LOCATION:LGBTQ+ CULTURE CENTER
GEO:39.168722;-86.525274
SUMMARY:The Importance of Voting for the LGBTQ+ Community
DESCRIPTION:Make Your Voice Heard!                                  Join 
 us for an evening of conversation\, learning\, and community as we explor
 e the power of voting and civic engagement in shaping a more inclusive fu
 ture for LGBTQ+ communities. Our guest speaker\, Professor Steve Sanders\
 , will share insights on the history of voting rights\, the impact of col
 lective action\, and why participation in the 2026 election matters. Whet
 her you're a first-time voter or a longtime advocate\, you'll have the op
 portunity to ask questions\, share perspectives\, and connect with others
  who are passionate about making a difference.                           
      Steve Sanders is Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and Professor o
 f Law in the Maurer School of Law at IU Bloomington. He holds additional 
 appointments as an Adjunct Professor of Political Science and an affiliat
 ed faculty member with the Department of Gender Studies and the Kinsey In
 stitute. Steve's primary teaching area is Constitutional Law\, and his sc
 holarship focuses on questions arising out of the Fourteenth Amendment's 
 guarantees of equal protection and due process\, with a special focus on 
 issues affecting LGBTQ persons and same-sex couples. Steve developed and 
 taught IU's first course on "Gay and Lesbian Politics" in 1996\, chaired 
 the committee that won approval for domestic partner benefits in 2001\, a
 nd was a longtime member of the board of the IU LGBTQ+ Alumni Association
 . He has received a Leadership Award from Lambda Legal and is a three-tim
 e winner of the IU Trustees Teaching Award.Ready to take action? Register
  to vote! Visit www.indianavoters.in.gov to check your registration statu
 s or register to vote (you can also click on the "register" button below)
 . Follow the LGBTQ+ Culture Center on QNews\, Facebook\, and Instagram fo
 r voter registration updates\, election information\, and important deadl
 ines. The deadline to register to vote in Indiana is October 5\, 2026.   
                                Come learn\, connect\, and take the next s
 tep toward making your voice count.                                All In
 diana University events\, groups\, activities\, educational\, cultural\, 
 and historical observances welcome all members of the Indiana University 
 community.                                  &#160\;
